<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75500" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄρχις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιος</span> and
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>, ὁ, 
			Att.
		 nom. pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄρχεις,</span>
		
			Ion.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄρχιες,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>testicle,</i> freq. in pl.,
				<i>testicles,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.109
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
			</span></i><i>Aër.</i><i><span class="en">
				4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eub.
				63.4
			</span></i> (anap.), etc. ; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄσχις.</span>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in females, <i>ovaries,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				2.810
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> plant so
			called from the form of its root, <i>salep, Orchis
			papilionacea,</i> and <i>O. longicruris,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				9.18.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				3.126
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄρχις, ἡ,</span>
			a kind of <i>olive,</i> Colum.<i><span class="en">
				5.8
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρχάς</span> (B). (Cf.
			Avest. <i>arazi</i> 'testicles'.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
